85-prove deployment. DEV-74's local acceptance review owns the complete connection
86-qualification; T009 retains safe exported tracing. The Bun commands and public contract
87-stay available during this work.
88-
89:## Analytics candidate
90-
91-`src/calculator-analytics.layer.ts` adds one application owner after a native
92-hosted calculation succeeds. It collects only the catalogue calculator ID and
93-name. HTTP, native RPC and the two MCP protocols use this same decorator;
94-pure tax packages and local SDK calls have no analytics dependency. Metadata,
95-failed or interrupted calculations add no successful-use event. A request can
96-collect at most 64 successes; excess analytics are dropped without changing
97-the calculation. This bounded loss does not promise an exact count under loss.
98-
99-`src/analytics-request.boundary.ts` uses the private analytics package’s shared
100-header boundary to read the optional collection choice once.
101-Missing means allow; deny, malformed values or `DNT: 1` mean no collection.
102-The policy carries no browser identity and changes neither admission nor the
103-existing rate key. The native MCP registration omits the request collector;
104-the older session host makes a fresh collector for each incoming request.
105-
106-The native application composes the private
107-[analytics backend](../../packages/analytics/README.md). After a completed
108-bounded response, native Worker or session `waitUntil` schedules the one-attempt
109-send. The send owns its HTTP scope and deadline. Expected capture errors have
110-fixed safe diagnostics and do not change the response. Off is the default;
111-invalid enabled settings become a fixed native Config error. An in-process
112-host has no background delivery. The retained standalone Bun host remains
113-local and does not acquire analytics.
114-
115-T008 is still in progress. Focused tests cover the event owner, request
116-isolation, policies and controlled transport. The built native API additionally
117-checks real Fetch sends after HTTP and RPC calculations and both official MCP
118-client protocols. Each MCP conversation changes deny → allow → deny without
119-retaining its first choice. Rejected or redirected capture keeps the tax reply
120-successful; a stalled capture reply reaches the native five-second drop while
121-the tax reply returns within two seconds. The controlled Node response bridge
122-does not expose upstream body cancellation; that is not claimed.
123-
124-The Website forwards a fresh browser preference or original HTML request choice
125-to this same boundary. Its built-pair proof is recorded in the
126-[Website policy receipt](../../docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-calculator-collection-policy.json).
127-Browser sender privacy, retained provider projects and stored UUID readback
128-still require their remaining tests and separately qualified provider journey. The
129-[candidate receipt](../../docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-analytics-backend-and-request-policy.json)
